const MOVIES_BASE = [{"num": 1, "t": "My Neighbor Totoro", "y": "1988", "la": "5+", "ca": "5+", "full": "Gentle and whimsical, but not emotionally weightless. The girls' mother is ill and hospitalized (nothing graphic, but real worry), and there's a tense sequence where the younger sister goes missing. A mother scolds her son harshly early on. Totoro himself and the \"dust sprites\" might look odd but are quickly shown to be friendly, not scary. A nonsexual bathing scene shows a family in a soaking tub with brief partial nudity (bare shoulders/chests/legs). Strong themes of sibling bonds, courage, and compassion.", "genre": ["Animation", "Fantasy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Studio Ghibli"}, {"num": 2, "t": "Finding Nemo", "y": "2003", "la": "5+", "ca": "6+", "full": "No traditional villain, but real tension: the opening shows Nemo's mother and siblings-to-be killed by a predator (quick, not graphic, but a gut-punch for sensitive kids). Nemo is separated from his father and nearly dies more than once; Marlin faces sharks, jellyfish, and an anglerfish in genuinely scary scenes. Themes of overprotection, letting go, and perseverance run throughout. Fine for many 5-6 year olds, but the shark and jellyfish sequences catch some kids off guard.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Comedy"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 3, "t": "A Bug's Life", "y": "1998", "la": "5+", "ca": "6+", "full": "More intense than its G rating suggests. Grasshoppers led by Hopper menace and threaten the ant colony with real bullying and violence; there's fire, rain, and predatory birds. Not gory, but the sustained threat and aggressive language surprise some parents. Positive messages about teamwork, individuality, and standing up to bullies.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Comedy"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 4, "t": "Toy Story", "y": "1995", "la": "5+", "ca": "6+", "full": "Tense/scary moments played mostly for humor: toys get knocked around, dismembered-arm slapstick, a squeaky alien toy torn apart by Sid's dog. Sid himself mutilates and reassembles toys into unsettling \"mutant\" hybrids that can frighten younger or sensitive kids, and Scud the dog is genuinely menacing. A dad is shown asleep next to beer cans. Core messages: courage, teamwork, humility, and outgrowing rivalry for friendship.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Comedy"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 5, "t": "Paddington", "y": "2014", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "CSM recommends this warm live-action/CGI comedy for age 6+. Concerns: some peril (a taxidermist villain wants to stuff Paddington), slapstick, and mild scares; very little language, no sex, minimal substances. Positive themes: kindness, family, welcoming immigrants and outsiders, politeness, and that \"in London everyone is different, so anyone can fit in.\"", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Comedy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 6, "t": "Charlotte's Web", "y": "2006", "la": "5+", "ca": "5+", "full": "CSM praises this adaptation as unusually respectful of E.B. White's classic. The chief concern is the death of a central character (Charlotte), handled with appropriate mourning and recovery, plus references to the farmer's plan to slaughter Wilbur. Templeton the rat models selfishness. No language/sex/substance issues. Positive: friendship, loyalty, the cycle of life, selflessness.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Drama", "Comedy"], "studio": "Paramount"}, {"num": 7, "t": "Shaun the Sheep Movie", "y": "2015", "la": "5+", "ca": "5+", "full": "\"Tons of barn-animal fun in sweet stop-motion adventure,\" told with no dialogue. Appropriate for older preschoolers mature enough to handle brief mild peril (a cruel animal-control officer with an electrified claw device). Some potty humor (fart, burp, poop jokes) and a gag where a man flirts with two sheep in disguise. Positive: teamwork, friendship, fixing your mistakes.", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy"], "studio": "Aardman"}, {"num": 8, "t": "The Good Dinosaur", "y": "2015", "la": "6+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Young dino braves nature in lovely but intense adventure.\" CSM's 8+ is well above the list's 6+: it flags many scenes of peril, trauma, and loss — including the death of Arlo's father, flash floods, and animal attacks — plus a hallucination sequence after characters eat rotten fruit. Likely to frighten younger/sensitive viewers. Positive: courage, family, loyalty, facing fears.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 9, "t": "Ponyo", "y": "2008", "la": "5+", "ca": "5+", "full": "\"Miyazaki's stunning adventure is geared to younger kids\" — one of his most kid-friendly films. Concerns: fantasy peril during tsunami/flood sequences and moments when Sosuke fears Ponyo is lost; a slightly scary wizard father. Minimal language, no sex or substances. Positive: strong female characters, loyalty, love, environmental balance, a 5-year-old modeling responsibility.", "genre": ["Animation", "Fantasy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Studio Ghibli"}, {"num": 10, "t": "Inside Out", "y": "2015", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Creative, clever story about big feelings has peril, scares.\" CSM notes some peril and scary moments (e.g., a frightening subconscious sequence, the loss of an imaginary friend) and heavy themes about sadness/depression that can overwhelm younger kids. A passing mention of a mom's former boyfriend. Positive: all emotions matter; empathy, family, and honest feelings.", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 11, "t": "Encanto", "y": "2021", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Vibrant visuals, catchy songs, moving messages.\" Concerns are mild: some thematic elements and peril (the off-screen murder of a man in front of his wife in backstory, frightening visions, a crumbling house), plus a kid drinking coffee and a family toast. No real language or sex. Positive: family, self-acceptance, generational healing, Colombian culture.", "genre": ["Animation", "Musical", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 12, "t": "Luca", "y": "2021", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Sweet fish-out-of-water story about friendship, adventure.\" Concerns: near-attacks on sea monsters with harpoons, some peril, rude humor, and mild name-calling; some parents flag disobedience themes. No sex; minimal substances. Positive: courage, curiosity, empathy, perseverance, teamwork, and friendship on the Italian Riviera.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Comedy"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 13, "t": "Zootopia", "y": "2016", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Charming buddy-animal story promotes teamwork, perseverance.\" CSM's 8+ reflects several scenes of danger and tension, predators who \"go savage\" (including a frightening black jaguar), and mature commentary on prejudice, policing, and sexism. Also flags a fatphobic portrayal of one officer. Minimal language/sex/substances. Positive: teamwork, tolerance, perseverance, questioning stereotypes.", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Mystery"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 14, "t": "How to Train Your Dragon", "y": "2010", "la": "6+", "ca": "7+", "full": "\"Thrilling adventure sends brains-over-brawn message.\" Concerns: scary-looking dragons, destruction, and battle sequences; characters drink from mugs in a bar-style setting; a crush/date subplot. Limb differences in central characters are handled sensitively. Positive: compassion, integrity, perseverance, and that strategy and empathy beat brute force.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Fantasy"], "studio": "DreamWorks"}, {"num": 15, "t": "Over the Moon", "y": "2020", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Dreamy, China-set musical fairy tale has positive lessons.\" The fantasy violence is only mildly scary; the heavier material is a dying mother and a \"Chamber of Exquisite Sadness,\" which resolve into growth. Some flirting/romance between the father and his new partner. No language/substances. Positive: processing grief, girls in STEM, family, that loving new people doesn't erase old love.", "genre": ["Animation", "Musical", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Netflix"}, {"num": 16, "t": "March of the Penguins", "y": "2005", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Stunning, loving documentary; some intense peril.\" CSM flags occasionally disturbing imagery of penguins walking, mating, and dying, including chicks and eggs lost to cold and predators. No language/sex/substances. Positive: perseverance, devoted parenting, teamwork, and reverence for nature.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Documentary"], "studio": "Warner Bros."}, {"num": 17, "t": "March of the Penguins 2: The Next Step", "y": "2017", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Another beautiful, fascinating penguin docu; some peril,\" narrated by Morgan Freeman. Concerns: birds of prey attack and try to kill young Emperor penguins; discussion of climate change and possible penguin extinction, handled without heavy-handedness. Positive: cooperative parenting, perseverance, reverence for nature, the cycle of life.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Documentary"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 18, "t": "The LEGO Movie", "y": "2014", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Hilarious toy tale plugs product but is nonstop fun.\" Concerns: nonstop cartoonish action (chases, explosions aimed at plastic minifigures), a crush/love-triangle subplot with mild jealousy, and — most notably — heavy consumerism, since the film doubles as a LEGO commercial. Minimal language/substances. Positive: teamwork, creativity, individuality, that anyone can be \"special.\"", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Warner Bros."}, {"num": 19, "t": "Mary Poppins", "y": "1964", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "CSM says this classic musical is \"a fine movie for children of any age,\" listing it 6+ mostly for full plot comprehension. Only a handful of chaotic moments may briefly scare younger kids; death is mentioned; the father drinks sherry and mentions a pipe, and minor characters smoke. A married couple kisses. Positive: a strong, independent, caring nanny; family, imagination, compassion.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Musical", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 20, "t": "Mary Poppins Returns", "y": "2018", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Blunt is a delight in sweet, nostalgic, toe-tapping sequel.\" Concerns: a few suspenseful scenes and the significant thematic weight that Michael's wife has died a year earlier (the children sing about missing her). Off-screen tie-in merchandise. No real language/sex/substances. Positive: hope, family, grief and healing, finding joy; educational nods to the Great Depression.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Musical", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 21, "t": "Penguins", "y": "2019", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Funny narration makes Arctic docu particularly kid-friendly,\" narrated by Ed Helms. Concerns: predator peril (leopard seals, killer whales, skua birds threaten an Adélie penguin), but softened by comedic narration. No language/sex/substances. Positive: teamwork, perseverance, devoted parenting, nature appreciation.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Documentary"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 22, "t": "Up", "y": "2009", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Pixar's stunning adventure is an upper for everyone.\" CSM's PG-level concerns: a band of trained talking dogs menacing the heroes, near-falls from a floating house, and some gunfire; violence stays mild. Most notable is the deeply moving opening montage depicting a wife's death and the couple's inability to have children. Two adults sip champagne. Positive: love, loyalty, adventure at any age, found family.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Comedy"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 23, "t": "Vivo", "y": "2021", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "Touching Lin-Manuel Miranda animated musical. Concerns: some peril and scary scenes with a hungry giant snake and dogs chasing a small animal, plus a non-graphic death (a limp hand indicating a character has died). No language/sex/substances. Positive: family, love, following through on promises; strong Cuban/Latino representation.", "genre": ["Animation", "Musical", "Adventure"], "studio": "Sony Pictures Animation"}, {"num": 24, "t": "Smallfoot", "y": "2018", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "Animated musical about yetis. Concerns: lots of slapstick falls from heights (all survived), dart guns with sedatives, a plane crash, and a fear-driven flashback with weapons; mild flirting; a minor character drinks at a bar; infrequent \"crap\"/\"stupid.\" Positive: questioning authority, seeking truth, honesty, and understanding those who are different.", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Musical"], "studio": "Warner Bros."}, {"num": 25, "t": "Terra Willy", "y": "2019", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "French animated space-survival adventure (also called Astro Kid). Concerns: mild peril, a child emotionally separated from his parents, a few slightly scary aliens, and brief potty humor. No sex, language, or substances. Positive: curiosity, learning, emotional resilience, empathy, teamwork, and problem-solving.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Sci-Fi"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 26, "t": "Migration", "y": "2023", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Funny animated adventure is just ducky; some peril, threats.\" Concerns: action/peril, a menacing chef who threatens the ducks, and mild rude humor; brief flirting. Little other iffy content. Positive: family togetherness, courage, and opening yourself to new experiences.", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Illumination"}, {"num": 27, "t": "Muppets Most Wanted", "y": "2014", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Amusing Muppets sequel ups the gags, as well as the action.\" Concerns: comic action with some guns, a Siberian gulag storyline, and a villain (Constantine) that some younger kids find intense; mild language (\"hell\"/\"suck\"). Positive: teamwork, friendship, being yourself.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Comedy", "Musical"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 28, "t": "Singin' in the Rain", "y": "1952", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "CSM recommends this classic MGM musical comedy for about age 6+. Concerns are very mild: some slapstick, mild romantic flirting and kissing, and social drinking/smoking typical of its era. No real violence or crude content. Positive: perseverance, friendship, integrity (exposing a fraud), and joyful artistry.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Musical", "Comedy"], "studio": "MGM"}, {"num": 29, "t": "The Sound of Music", "y": "1965", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "CSM recommends this beloved musical for about age 6+. Concerns: the looming Nazi threat and the family's tense escape from Austria, plus some romantic content (kissing, an older teen romance) and social drinking. Positive: courage, family, standing up to tyranny, love, and music as resilience.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Musical", "Drama"], "studio": "20th Century Fox"}, {"num": 30, "t": "The Wizard of Oz", "y": "1939", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "CSM's tagline: \"One of the best family films ever made; has scary moments.\" It flags several scenes of peril, almost all involving the green-skinned Wicked Witch of the West and her band of creepy flying monkeys, plus a tornado and threatening imagery. No language/sex/substances of note. Positive: courage, friendship, resourcefulness, and \"there's no place like home.\"", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Musical", "Fantasy"], "studio": "MGM"}, {"num": 31, "t": "Paddington in Peru", "y": "2025", "la": "6+", "ca": "6+", "full": "The third Paddington film. Concerns: adventure action and some intense scenes that may disturb younger viewers, mild rude humor, a spider, and peril; a box of martini glasses/alcohol appears as \"emergency supplies,\" plus a suggestive one-liner. Positive: family, faith in yourself and loved ones, finding where you belong, kindness, courage.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Comedy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 32, "t": "The Boy, the Mole, the Fox and the Horse", "y": "2022", "la": "6+", "ca": "7+", "full": "CSM recommends this gentle Oscar-winning animated short for age 7+. Concerns: mild tension — the fox threatens to kill the mole, a character nearly drowns, and there's a winter storm. No language/sex/substances. Positive: kindness, self-worth, love, and friendship; the idea that \"home\" isn't a place.", "genre": ["Animation", "Drama", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 33, "t": "The Secret of Kells", "y": "2009", "la": "8+", "ca": "10+", "full": "\"Magical animated adventure is intense but beautiful.\" CSM's 10+ is well above the list's 8+: Viking/barbarian invaders terrorize and kill villagers with swords and axes, villages burn, red-eyed wolves snarl, and an evil pagan serpent god (Crom Cruach) appears. Positive: light overcomes darkness, the value of art and knowledge, and standing up for beliefs; rich Irish folklore.", "genre": ["Animation", "Fantasy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 34, "t": "Wreck-It Ralph", "y": "2012", "la": "7+", "ca": "7+", "full": "\"Game-themed movie mixes potty humor with strong messages.\" Concerns: a first-person-shooter game comes to life with alien bugs, some peril, a character pours a martini, a wedding kiss, and potty humor. Positive: perseverance, integrity, self-acceptance, teamwork, and \"there's no wrong side to be on.\"", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 35, "t": "Onward", "y": "2020", "la": "7+", "ca": "7+", "full": "\"Original, heartfelt sibling adventure about love and loss.\" Concerns: fantasy action/peril, a few mild scares (a Manticore, a monster), goofy/rude humor, and the heavy theme of grieving a dead father. Minimal language. Positive: brotherhood, teamwork, perseverance, and resilience.", "genre": ["Animation", "Fantasy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 36, "t": "E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial", "y": "1982", "la": "7+", "ca": "7+", "full": "CSM recommends Spielberg's classic for about age 7+, though its parents' guide notes the film \"features surprisingly strong language and scenes that may not be suitable for young viewers,\" leading some families to hold it until closer to 10. Concerns: intense scenes (E.T. appears near death, menacing government agents in hazmat suits), the emotional weight of a broken family and near-loss, and notable mild profanity for its era. Positive: friendship, empathy, childhood wonder, and loyalty.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Sci-Fi", "Adventure"], "studio": "Universal"}, {"num": 37, "t": "A Greyhound of a Girl", "y": "2024", "la": "7+", "ca": "7+", "full": "CSM recommends this \"sweet animated adaptation about losing a grandparent\" for age 7+. The central theme is death and grief — a grandmother approaching the end of her life. Mild Irish slang (\"eejit\") and \"Jesus\" as an exclamation. No sex/substances. Positive: adapting to loss, multi-generational family love, and that love endures.", "genre": ["Animation", "Drama", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 38, "t": "My Father's Dragon", "y": "2022", "la": "7+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Runaway finds courage in colorful cartoon fantasy adventure.\" Concerns: Elmer runs away distressed after his mother yells at him, some \"shut up\" and threats, and mild peril. No sex/substances. Positive: that a friend can see you through scary times; courage, resourcefulness, and friendship.", "genre": ["Animation", "Fantasy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Netflix"}, {"num": 39, "t": "Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone", "y": "2001", "la": "7+", "ca": "7+", "full": "CSM recommends the first Harry Potter for about age 7+. Concerns: fantasy peril and scary moments (a mountain troll, a three-headed dog, Voldemort emerging from the back of a head, a tense final confrontation) and the backstory of Harry's murdered parents. Minimal language/sex/substances. Positive: friendship, courage, loyalty, and standing up for what's right.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Fantasy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Warner Bros."}, {"num": 40, "t": "Felix and the Hidden Treasure", "y": "2021", "la": "7+", "ca": "6+", "full": "Canadian animated seafaring/sci-fi adventure. Concerns: mild cartoon violence, a mysterious cult subplot, a couple kissing, and the emotional weight of a father missing at sea. Positive: strong role models, determination, and family.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 41, "t": "Mighty Joe Young", "y": "1998", "la": "7+", "ca": "8+", "full": "CSM recommends this adventure about a giant gorilla for about age 8+. Concerns: action violence and peril (poachers with guns, a mother killed protecting her baby gorilla in the opening, a fire-filled climax) that can frighten younger kids. Mild language. Positive: conservation, courage, loyalty, protecting the vulnerable.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Adventure", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 42, "t": "Peter Pan (Broadway Musical)", "y": "2000", "la": "7+", "ca": "Not on CSM; substitute source used", "full": "This filmed stage production (the Cathy Rigby Broadway musical) does not have a dedicated Common Sense Media movie review. Drawing on the broader assessment of Peter Pan stage/screen adaptations: expect swashbuckling sword fights, a menacing but comedic Captain Hook, mild peril, and dated cultural depictions of Native Americans that warrant a parental conversation. Positive: imagination, bravery, friendship, and the bittersweet theme of growing up. Substitute assessment — no direct CSM page exists for this specific production; if you mean Disney's 1953 animated or the 2003 live-action film, each has its own CSM review with a different rating.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Musical", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 43, "t": "Strike", "y": "2020", "la": "7+", "ca": "~6+ (approximate)", "full": "British stop-motion about a mole who dreams of playing soccer but is destined to be a coal miner. Concerns: potty humor (burps/farts), slapstick, a cartoonishly evil villain, and a tragic mine-accident thread. Positive: pursuing your dreams, community, and brave, smart kids in non-traditional roles.", "genre": ["Animation", "Sports", "Comedy"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 44, "t": "The Princess Diaries", "y": "2001", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "CSM recommends this Disney comedy for about age 8+. Concerns: mild teen romance and kissing, some mean-girl bullying and social-status pressure, and light rude humor. Minimal substances. Positive: self-confidence, being true to yourself, responsibility, and inner beauty over appearances.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Comedy", "Romance"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 45, "t": "Yes Day", "y": "2021", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "CSM recommends this family comedy for about age 8+. Concerns: chaotic slapstick and some risky stunts (a theme-park ride, a car wash with windows down, a messy food fight), mild language, and a scene at a music festival. Positive: family bonding, trust, empathy between parents and kids, and balancing rules with fun.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Comedy"], "studio": "Netflix"}, {"num": 46, "t": "Ron's Gone Wrong", "y": "2021", "la": "8+", "ca": "9+ (approximate)", "full": "Animated comedy about a boy and his malfunctioning robot. Concerns: bullying, social-media/tech themes, some peril and crude humor (\"poop\"), a reference to vodka, and adults with sparkling wine. Positive: real vs. online friendship, being yourself, and healthy technology use.", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Sci-Fi"], "studio": "20th Century Fox"}, {"num": 47, "t": "The Bad Guys", "y": "2022", "la": "8+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Book-based animated heist is so fun, it's criminal.\" Concerns: cartoon violence (characters hit by a car, explosions, self-defense fighting) and momentary peril; cocktail/champagne glasses at a gala. Positive: the harm of stereotypes, redemption, teamwork, and choosing to do good.", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Action"], "studio": "DreamWorks"}, {"num": 48, "t": "Raya and the Last Dragon", "y": "2021", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Fantasy adventure has girl power, action, emotion.\" CSM's 8+ reflects scary sequences and intense fights against relentless plague-like Druun monsters that turn people to stone, plus a major theme of grief and broken trust. Some name-calling. Positive: trust, teamwork, courage, perseverance, and Southeast Asian representation (with the caveat that cultures are blended non-specifically).", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 49, "t": "Soul", "y": "2020", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Amazing animation, serious themes in thoughtful dramedy.\" Concerns: a man nearly dies (his body appears dead/dying), heavy existential themes about death, the afterlife, and life's meaning; some mild language and a kiss. Positive: purpose, living in the moment, mentorship; Pixar's first Black lead.", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Drama"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 50, "t": "Abominable", "y": "2019", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Funny, heartwarming adventure has some peril, scares.\" Concerns: a yeti and three kids pursued by armed adults in vehicles, some peril/scares, grief over a father's death, and mild rude humor. Positive: teamwork, compassion, friendship, and healing from grief; Chinese setting and characters.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Fantasy"], "studio": "DreamWorks"}, {"num": 51, "t": "Wish Dragon", "y": "2021", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"China-set animated comedy has great messages, some scares.\" Concerns: lots of animated fights and falls from great heights, characters who die and are revived, kung-fu chases; adults drink wine/champagne, a woman flirts and kisses; mild insults and a toilet gag. Positive: friendship earned, humility, compassion, and that wealth and fame don't bring happiness.", "genre": ["Animation", "Fantasy", "Comedy"], "studio": "Sony Pictures Animation"}, {"num": 52, "t": "Spies in Disguise", "y": "2019", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "Animated spy buddy comedy. Concerns: action violence (fighting, weapons, some injuries and at least two deaths, a reference to an officer killed in the line of duty), a brief partial-nudity gag, and mild language. Positive: teamwork, accepting help, and promoting non-lethal, non-violent ways to stop criminals.", "genre": ["Animation", "Action", "Comedy"], "studio": "Blue Sky Studios"}, {"num": 53, "t": "The Mitchells vs. the Machines", "y": "2021", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "Animated robot-apocalypse comedy. Concerns: lots of cartoonish action (robots crushed/impaled, oil as \"blood\"), a groin-kick gag, a brief obscured-nudity joke, and mild language. Positive: family unity, understanding differences, and appreciating others' perspectives; features positive LGBTQ+ representation (a lesbian teen protagonist).", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Sci-Fi"], "studio": "Sony Pictures Animation"}, {"num": 54, "t": "Wolfwalkers", "y": "2020", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Lush, lyrical Irish folktale has dark moments, peril.\" Concerns: sequences of violence and scary images — wolves bite and scratch people, characters are shot with crossbows (some mild blood), a character falls to their death, and villagers threaten wolves with cannons and swords; brief \"bloody hell\" and religious exclamations. Positive: empathy, courage, tolerance, environmentalism, and standing up to authority.", "genre": ["Animation", "Fantasy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 55, "t": "The Sea Beast", "y": "2022", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Swashbuckling adventure has kid role model, monster attacks.\" Concerns: animated action violence, scary giant sea-monster attacks that destroy ships, and some peril; monster hunters share flasks of alcohol; mild insults. Positive: questioning official history and propaganda, that there's more than meets the eye, courage; a Black girl lead.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Netflix"}, {"num": 56, "t": "The One and Only Ivan", "y": "2020", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Big-hearted adaptation should please fans of the book.\" Concerns: mild thematic elements — circus animals in captivity, the death of an elephant, and some sadness (softened from the book). A car-brand product placement. Positive: loyal friendship, teamwork, empathy, perseverance, redemption, and animal welfare.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Drama", "Adventure"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 57, "t": "Flora & Ulysses", "y": "2021", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "Comedy about a girl and a superhero squirrel. Concerns: action played for humor (a squirrel causes mayhem, an animal-control agent fires tranquilizer darts, a cat attack leaves bloody scratches, a near car crash), divorced/separated parents, adults drinking wine, and sensual romance-novel covers on a wall. Positive: hope in hard times, family, friendship, and perseverance.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Comedy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 58, "t": "The Biggest Little Farm", "y": "2018", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "CSM recommends this acclaimed farming documentary for about age 8+. Concerns: real farm life including animal death (predator attacks, animals that don't survive) and some peril that may upset sensitive kids. No language/sex/substances of note. Positive: ecological harmony, resilience, perseverance, sustainable agriculture, and following a dream.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Documentary"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 59, "t": "The Biggest Little Farm: The Return", "y": "2022", "la": "8+", "ca": "~7–8+ (approximate)", "full": "An Earth Day mini-documentary follow-up. Concerns: real farm life including animal death (e.g., piglets that don't survive) and animals in peril, which may upset sensitive kids. Positive: nature's ecosystems, resilience, perseverance, sustainable farming, and family.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Documentary"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 60, "t": "Jane", "y": "2017", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "CSM recommends this documentary about Jane Goodall for about age 8+. Concerns: some real footage of chimpanzee aggression, illness (a polio outbreak among the chimps), and death in the wild; mature discussion of Goodall's marriage and career sacrifices. No language/substance issues. Positive: perseverance, scientific curiosity, conservation, and a groundbreaking female scientist as a role model.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Documentary", "Biography"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 61, "t": "Dream Big: Engineering Our World", "y": "2017", "la": "8+", "ca": "~8+ (approximate)", "full": "IMAX STEM documentary narrated by Jeff Bridges. Concerns are essentially none — no violence, language, or sex; a couple of engineers reference difficult pasts. Positive: strong STEM/educational value, engineering as a force for good, and inspiring female-engineer role models.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Documentary"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 62, "t": "Paper Planes", "y": "2014", "la": "8+", "ca": "10+", "full": "\"Thoughtful, inspired look at grief soars.\" CSM's 10+ exceeds the list's 8+: concerns include a boy pushing another down stairs, mild bullying, a mother killed in a car accident (grief), a boy stealing from his dad, a hungover father, and mild language (\"hell,\" \"sucks\"). Positive: perseverance, standing up to bullies, sportsmanship, and processing grief at your own pace.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Sports", "Drama"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 63, "t": "The Eagle Huntress", "y": "2016", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "CSM recommends this inspiring documentary about 13-year-old Aisholpan, the first female eagle hunter in her Mongolian Kazakh family, for age 8+. Concerns: some real hunting sequences (a sheep's throat is slit, foxes are hunted), edited for tension. Positive: girl power, dedication, perseverance, discipline, and a remarkable father-daughter relationship.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Documentary"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 64, "t": "Elemental", "y": "2023", "la": "8+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Heartfelt, romantic fable about immigrant experience.\" Concerns: mild peril (explosive fire bursts, a climactic flood), discriminatory comments toward fire people (\"go back to Fireland\"), insults, and swearing stand-ins (\"lazy ash\"); more romance than usual for Pixar (a young-adult couple flirt and kiss). Positive: the immigrant experience, acceptance, breaking down prejudice, family, and cross-cultural love.", "genre": ["Animation", "Fantasy", "Romance"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 65, "t": "We Can Be Heroes", "y": "2020", "la": "8+", "ca": "8+", "full": "Robert Rodriguez superhero-kids adventure. Concerns: mild fantasy/action violence (kids and adults fighting aliens/monsters), an alien-invasion premise with captured parents that may scare young kids, one brief cleavage shot, and mild language. No substances/sex. Positive: teamwork, child empowerment, and discovering your strengths.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Superhero", "Action"], "studio": "Netflix"}, {"num": 66, "t": "A Beautiful Planet", "y": "2016", "la": "8+", "ca": "~7+ (approximate)", "full": "IMAX documentary of Earth filmed from the International Space Station, narrated by Jennifer Lawrence. Concerns are minimal — no violence, language, or sex; the film discusses climate change and human environmental impact, which is thematically mature but not frightening. Positive: strong educational/STEM value, environmental stewardship, and global perspective.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Documentary"], "studio": "Warner Bros."}, {"num": 67, "t": "Willy Wonka & the Chocolate Factory", "y": "1971", "la": "8+", "ca": "6+", "full": "CSM lists this musical classic for about age 6+, though it flags genuinely unsettling moments: the psychedelic, nightmarish boat-tunnel scene, bratty children meeting alarming fates, and a generally dark undertone. Some mild peril and scares. Positive: honesty, humility, and that good character is rewarded over greed.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Musical", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Warner Bros."}, {"num": 68, "t": "Finding 'Ohana", "y": "2021", "la": "9+", "ca": "9+", "full": "\"Fun Hawaii adventure celebrates culture; peril, language.\" Concerns: treasure-hunt peril (venomous spider bites, caves and skeletons, a near-drowning requiring CPR, \"Night Marchers\" spirits), language (\"stupid,\" \"sucks,\" anatomical/potty references), and tween flirting/a kiss. Positive: family ('ohana), Hawaiian language, culture, and heritage, identity, and teamwork.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Adventure", "Comedy"], "studio": "Netflix"}, {"num": 69, "t": "Kubo and the Two Strings", "y": "2016", "la": "9+", "ca": "9+", "full": "Stop-motion fantasy set in ancient Japan. Concerns: dark thematic elements including death, scary images (a tentacled sea monster, sinister evil Sisters, the Moon King), and action/peril; a mother's sacrifice and death. Positive: storytelling, family, memory, resilience, and honoring loved ones.", "genre": ["Animation", "Fantasy", "Adventure"], "studio": "Laika"}, {"num": 70, "t": "The Princess Bride", "y": "1987", "la": "9+", "ca": "8+", "full": "CSM's tagline: \"Witty, winsome fairy tale has violence, language.\" Recommended for about age 8+. Concerns: swordfighting, a torture machine, R.O.U.S. (rodents of unusual size), some peril and mild scares, and a bit of innuendo; brief kissing and some mild language. Positive: true love, loyalty, friendship, courage, and wit over brawn.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Fantasy", "Adventure"], "studio": "20th Century Fox"}, {"num": 71, "t": "The Sandlot", "y": "1993", "la": "9+", "ca": "9+", "full": "CSM's tagline: \"Lighthearted tween baseball comedy has language, sexism.\" Recommended for age 9+. Concerns: period-typical strong language and insults, kids chewing tobacco and getting sick, a mild sexual reference/a lifeguard kiss ruse, and a menacing dog. Positive: friendship, belonging, teamwork, and childhood adventure.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Sports", "Coming-of-Age"], "studio": "20th Century Fox"}, {"num": 72, "t": "Zarafa", "y": "2012", "la": "9+", "ca": "9+", "full": "\"Enchanting African fable with some scares and sadness\" (French, subtitled). Concerns: an orphaned boy, a slavery/slave-trader pursuit, some peril and sadness, and a man disoriented while smoking a long pipe. Positive: that personal freedom is worth fighting for, keeping promises, loyalty, and compassion; historical and cultural value.", "genre": ["Animation", "Adventure", "Drama"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 73, "t": "The Colors Within", "y": "2025", "la": "9+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Moving coming-of-age story about friendship and music\" (Japanese anime by Naoko Yamada). Concerns: very little iffy content — a teen is briefly knocked down in dodgeball, teens are disciplined for a sleepover, and there's gossip about a girl leaving school. No language/substances. Positive: found family, art and music, honesty, and staying true to yourself; synesthesia representation and Catholic-school prayer themes.", "genre": ["Animation", "Drama", "Musical"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 74, "t": "Dog Man", "y": "2025", "la": "9+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Amusing adaptation is true to book's silly humor, slapstick.\" Concerns: cartoon violence (Dog Man is surgically created from an officer and his dog, with brief stitches shown), the catchphrase \"See you later, suckers!,\" and mild potty/rude humor; two adults briefly express romantic feelings. Heavy off-screen merchandising. Positive: kindness and character strengths; a fairly diverse human cast.", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Action"], "studio": "DreamWorks"}, {"num": 75, "t": "Elio", "y": "2025", "la": "9+", "ca": "6+", "full": "\"Moments of peril in heartfelt adventure about lonely boy\" (Pixar). Concerns: sci-fi violence/peril (camp bullying, an alien emperor threatening destruction, a punch, a briefly scary toothy alien, a lava-pool threat, a bloody nose), the heavy theme of an orphaned boy grieving his parents, and mild language (\"stupid,\" \"butt\"); an adult drinks wine. Positive: courage, empathy, and being true to yourself; a diverse boy-of-color lead.", "genre": ["Animation", "Sci-Fi", "Adventure"], "studio": "Pixar"}, {"num": 76, "t": "How to Train Your Dragon (live-action)", "y": "2025", "la": "9+", "ca": "9+", "full": "CSM recommends the live-action remake for age 9+. Concerns: sequences of intense fantasy action and peril — dragons breathe fire into crowds, Vikings are thrown and smashed, weapons abound, a major character is injured, and there's a terrifying giant dragon (the Red Death); mild romance/a kiss, a \"breast hat\" joke, and \"bloody.\" Positive: friendship, courage, acceptance, and challenging tradition and prejudice.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Adventure", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Universal"}, {"num": 77, "t": "Liyana", "y": "2017", "la": "9+", "ca": "11+", "full": "\"Inspiring, unique film tells two stories of perseverance.\" CSM's 11+ is well above the list's 9+: this documentary about Swazi (eSwatini) orphans creating a fairy tale incorporates their real experiences of child abuse, alcoholic fathers, HIV, and armed men abducting children at night, plus scary animated elements. Positive: resilience, creativity, perseverance, hope — \"you write your own ending.\"", "genre": ["Documentary", "Animation"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 78, "t": "The Boy Who Harnessed the Wind", "y": "2019", "la": "10+", "ca": "11+", "full": "CSM recommends this true-story drama (set in Malawi) for about age 11+. Concerns: a harrowing famine, desperation and a near-riot over food, some violence, a dog's death, and mature themes of poverty and political corruption; some language. Positive: perseverance, ingenuity, education, family, and using science (a wind turbine) to save a community.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Drama", "Biography"], "studio": "Netflix"}, {"num": 79, "t": "If You Build It", "y": "2013", "la": "10+", "ca": "~10+ (approximate)", "full": "Inspiring documentary in which two designer-educators teach rural North Carolina high-schoolers to design and build a farmers' market. Concerns are very mild — a few scenes of adults drinking beer and some mild bickering; no swearing, smoking, drugs, sex, or violence. Positive: teamwork, perseverance, empowering youth, hands-on education, and community.", "genre": ["Documentary", "Live-Action"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 80, "t": "Queen of Katwe", "y": "2016", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "CSM recommends this Disney true-story drama about a Ugandan chess prodigy for about age 10+. Concerns: mature themes of extreme poverty, illness, a difficult childbirth, some peril and a near-assault, and family hardship. Minimal language. Positive: perseverance, education, self-belief, family, and breaking out of poverty through talent and mentorship.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Drama", "Biography"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 81, "t": "The Inventor: Out for Blood in Silicon Valley", "y": "2019", "la": "10+", "ca": "15+ (approximate)", "full": "Alex Gibney documentary on Elizabeth Holmes and the Theranos fraud. Concerns: themes of large-scale fraud, betrayal, and institutional failure, plus mild profanity; no sex, substances, or graphic violence, but a dry, interview-driven, mature subject that far exceeds the list's 10+ label. Positive: media literacy, critical thinking, and ethical whistleblowing.", "genre": ["Documentary", "Live-Action", "Biography"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 82, "t": "Girl Rising", "y": "2013", "la": "10+", "ca": "11+", "full": "CSM recommends this documentary about girls' education in the developing world for about age 11+. Concerns: mature real-world themes including child slavery, forced marriage, sexual abuse, and extreme poverty, presented seriously though not graphically. Positive: girls' empowerment, the transformative power of education, resilience, and global awareness.", "genre": ["Documentary", "Live-Action"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 83, "t": "Chasing Coral", "y": "2017", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "CSM recommends this Netflix environmental documentary about coral-reef bleaching for about age 10+. Concerns: no violence/language/sex; the mature, potentially distressing theme is the large-scale death of coral reefs due to climate change. Positive: strong STEM/environmental value, scientific perseverance, and urgency about climate action.", "genre": ["Documentary", "Live-Action"], "studio": "Netflix"}, {"num": 84, "t": "He Named Me Malala", "y": "2015", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "CSM recommends this documentary about Malala Yousafzai for about age 10+. Concerns: the Taliban's shooting of Malala and its aftermath, discussion of terrorism and oppression of girls, and some disturbing news footage. Positive: courage, girls' education and rights, activism, family, and standing up to extremism.", "genre": ["Documentary", "Live-Action", "Biography"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 85, "t": "Science Fair", "y": "2018", "la": "10+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Compelling, entertaining docu about teen science geniuses.\" Concerns: minimal — a brief description of microcephaly with footage of an affected baby may disturb some, and younger kids may not grasp the science. No language/sex/substances of note. Positive: STEM inspiration, perseverance, curiosity, thinking big, and a globally diverse group of student competitors.", "genre": ["Documentary", "Live-Action"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 86, "t": "My Octopus Teacher", "y": "2020", "la": "10+", "ca": "8+", "full": "CSM recommends this Oscar-winning nature documentary for about age 8+. Concerns: the \"circle of life\" in the kelp forest — a shark attacks and injures the octopus, and the octopus eventually dies (which can sadden viewers); some non-sexual nudity as the diver free-dives. Positive: nature connection, mindfulness, perseverance, empathy for other species, and environmental appreciation.", "genre": ["Documentary", "Live-Action"], "studio": "Netflix"}, {"num": 87, "t": "Night of the Zoopocalypse", "y": "2025", "la": "10+", "ca": "8+", "full": "\"Fun 'starter' horror flick has scary parts, positive themes.\" Concerns: zombie-like glowing-eyed mutant animals, many chases and frightening moments (a zombified grandmother tries to bite and turn her granddaughter, and is punched), and tranquilizer darts; insults (\"stupid,\" \"numbskull\"). Notably, no animals actually die. Positive: teamwork, courage, compassion, found family, and tolerance.", "genre": ["Animation", "Comedy", "Horror"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 88, "t": "Back to the Future", "y": "1985", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "CSM's guide notes this \"1980s time-travel favorite includes scenes in which main character Marty McFly and his friends are in physical jeopardy.\" Concerns: an attempted sexual assault played partly for comedy (Marty's mother's unwitting romantic interest in her own son), some violence including terrorists shooting a character, mild-to-moderate language, and teen drinking/smoking typical of the era. Positive: family, self-confidence, ingenuity, and standing up to bullies.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Sci-Fi", "Comedy"], "studio": "Universal"}, {"num": 89, "t": "School of Rock", "y": "2003", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "CSM recommends this Jack Black comedy for about age 10+. Concerns: frequent mild language and insults, a con-artist adult lying to kids and their school, rock-and-roll references to partying, and some rude humor. Positive: creativity, self-expression, teamwork, confidence, and mentorship (with the caveat that the hero starts as a liar).", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Comedy", "Musical"], "studio": "Paramount"}, {"num": 90, "t": "The Karate Kid", "y": "1984", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "CSM's tagline: \"1980s classic has fighting but still fun for older tweens.\" Recommended for age 10+. Concerns: significant bullying and martial-arts violence (a gang of teens repeatedly beats up the hero, a near-strangling), some strong language, and teen romance/drinking. Positive: discipline, mentorship, perseverance, self-defense over aggression, and balance in life.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Drama", "Sports"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 91, "t": "The Kid Who Would Be King", "y": "2019", "la": "10+", "ca": "9+", "full": "CSM recommends this Arthurian adventure for about age 9+. Concerns: fantasy action and scary imagery — flaming skeletal knights, a demonic sorceress (Morgana), and some peril; mild language and bullying. Positive: leadership, courage, teamwork, chivalry (\"a knight's code\"), and that ordinary kids can be heroes.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Fantasy", "Adventure"], "studio": "20th Century Fox"}, {"num": 92, "t": "Holes", "y": "2003", "la": "10+", "ca": "11+", "full": "CSM's tagline: \"Gritty adaptation of bestselling novel has violence.\" Recommended for age 11+. Violent flashbacks include the lynching of a Black man and men trying to force themselves onto women; other concerns include a harsh juvenile detention camp, cruelty by adults, deadly yellow-spotted lizards, gunfire, racism, and some language. Positive: friendship, loyalty, justice, breaking a family \"curse,\" and standing up to cruelty.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Adventure", "Mystery"], "studio": "Disney"}, {"num": 93, "t": "Hidden Figures", "y": "2016", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "CSM recommends this acclaimed true-story drama for about age 10+. Concerns: pervasive 1960s racism and segregation (slurs and discrimination), some tense workplace and historical moments, and mild language. Positive: perseverance, education, dignity, civil rights, and three Black women mathematicians as powerful STEM role models.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Drama", "Biography"], "studio": "20th Century Fox"}, {"num": 94, "t": "Little Women", "y": "2019", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "CSM recommends Greta Gerwig's adaptation for about age 10+. Concerns: the emotional weight of a sister's terminal illness and death, Civil War-era peril, some romance and heartbreak, and social drinking. Minimal language. Positive: sisterhood, female independence and ambition, family, artistic passion, and resilience.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Drama"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 95, "t": "Mixtape", "y": "2021", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "\"Serious themes, language in poignant tween dramedy.\" Concerns: mature themes — a 7th-grader's parents died in a car crash, ongoing grief, middle-school bullying, some fighting, a child not wearing a seatbelt treated casually, and some language. Positive: processing loss, self-discovery, connecting with family history, and friendship.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Comedy", "Coming-of-Age"], "studio": "Netflix"}, {"num": 96, "t": "Ride Like a Girl", "y": "2020", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "\"Woman gallops through boundaries in inspiring sports drama\" (a Michelle Payne biopic). Concerns: a parent has died off-screen and another character dies during the film; sexism and one instance of sexual harassment (advancement offered for sex); and disordered-eating imagery (an orange for dinner, plastic-wrap sweating to make weight). Positive: courage, perseverance, and breaking gender barriers; a respectful portrayal of a character with Down syndrome.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Drama", "Sports"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 97, "t": "Rainbow (Dhanak)", "y": "2016", "la": "10+", "ca": "~8+ (approximate)", "full": "Sweet Hindi road-trip fable in which a 10-year-old girl takes her blind younger brother across Rajasthan seeking a movie star to fund his eye surgery. Concerns: the threat of physical violence, a kidnapping, tense moments, smoking, alcohol, and parental death (the children are orphans). Positive: sibling love, faith, determination, kindness, and cross-cultural understanding.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Drama", "Adventure"], "studio": "Other"}, {"num": 98, "t": "Wonder", "y": "2017", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "CSM recommends this adaptation about a boy with facial differences for about age 10+. Concerns: significant bullying and cruelty, emotional distress, a pet dog's death, and some mild language. Positive: kindness (\"choose kind\"), empathy, inclusion, family, and seeing past appearances — one of the strongest pro-social messages on the list.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Drama", "Coming-of-Age"], "studio": "Lionsgate"}, {"num": 99, "t": "The Personal History of David Copperfield", "y": "2020", "la": "10+", "ca": "10+", "full": "CSM recommends this Dickens adaptation for about age 10+. Concerns: an abusive stepfather, child labor and poverty, some peril and period cruelty, a character's death, and social drinking. Minimal strong language. Positive: resilience, self-invention, kindness, found family, and the redemptive power of storytelling; a notably diverse, colorblind-cast production.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Comedy", "Drama"], "studio": "20th Century Fox"}, {"num": 100, "t": "The Water Man", "y": "2021", "la": "10+", "ca": "9+", "full": "David Oyelowo's directorial debut. Concerns: thematic content, scary images, and peril — a seriously ill mother (leukemia), a boy finding his mom's prescription morphine, two kids in danger in the woods, and an intense climax; touches on death and grief. Positive: honesty, courage, compassion, and strong parent-child bonds.", "genre": ["Live-Action", "Adventure", "Fantasy"], "studio": "Other"}];
